= Complex system — Technical =

== Interaction structure ==
Complex-system models commonly specify:

<pre>
components / agents
interaction topology
local dynamics
feedback
environment/boundary conditions
macro observables
</pre>

Collective behavior depends on the coupled dynamics rather than only isolated component properties.

== Modeling approaches ==
Methods include:

* dynamical systems;
* network science;
* agent-based models;
* statistical mechanics;
* stochastic processes;
* information-theoretic measures;
* multiscale/coarse-grained descriptions.

== Definition caution ==
Nonlinearity, emergence, heterogeneity, adaptation, and network structure are frequent but not individually necessary or sufficient across all definitions.

